Subject: Shrink and retry a refused mmap() reservation without ENABLE_MEMCHECK

libmdbx's default upper geometry scales with physical RAM: about 1.6x it, from
reasonable_db_maxsize(). osal_mmap() reserves that much address space up front.
Valgrind cannot map an arbitrarily large region, and its mmap() refuses one
that is too large with EINVAL. On CRAN's valgrind machine 0.1.1 failed
exactly there: every example and test opening an environment with the default
geometry stopped with "Invalid argument (mdbx error 22)" (issue #30). On a
16 GB GitHub runner the same open asks for ~20 GB, which valgrind maps, so the
package's own valgrind leg never saw it.

Upstream already handles this. osal_mmap() halves the reservation toward the
current size and retries while mmap() says EINVAL -- but only when
RUNNING_ON_ASAN or mdbx_running_on_Valgrind(), and the latter is constant 0
unless libmdbx is built with ENABLE_MEMCHECK and valgrind's headers. This
package is built with neither, and CRAN does not add them.

This patch drops that condition, so the retry runs on any EINVAL. Under
valgrind the environment opens with the largest reservation valgrind accepts;
env->geo_in_bytes.upper follows the mapping, as it already does in upstream's
ASAN builds, where this branch is live. Natively, Linux and macOS report an
oversized MAP_NORESERVE request as ENOMEM, not EINVAL, so the branch is not
reached; and if an EINVAL does arrive for another reason, the loop halves the
gap down to 1 MB -- a few dozen tries -- and then returns the EINVAL as before.

Rejected alternative: a package-level default map_size. It would change the
default geometry everywhere to fix one checker, and how map sizing is exposed
is an open design question (.agents/design.md).

Rejected alternative: -DENABLE_MEMCHECK. Tried for the CI leg and reverted
(see the header of tools/valgrind.supp, removed in 0.1.2): it needs <valgrind/memcheck.h> at build time,
raised the uninitialised-value reports from 2 contexts to 13, and shrinks the
default geometry to RAM/8 under valgrind.

--- a/src/vendor/libmdbx/mdbx.c
+++ b/src/vendor/libmdbx/mdbx.c
@@ -31792,7 +31792,11 @@
   if (unlikely(map->base == MAP_FAILED)) {
     err = errno;
     ASSERT(err != 0);
-    if ((RUNNING_ON_ASAN || mdbx_running_on_Valgrind()) && err == EINVAL && map->limit - map->current > MEGABYTE) {
+    /* R package patch: shrink and retry on any EINVAL, not only when built
+     * with ENABLE_MEMCHECK and running on Valgrind. This package is not built
+     * with it, yet CRAN runs it under Valgrind, whose mmap() refuses a
+     * reservation as large as the RAM-scaled default. See tools/patches. */
+    if (err == EINVAL && map->limit - map->current > MEGABYTE) {
       map->limit -= (map->limit - map->current) / 2;
       map->limit = max_unsigned(size, floor_powerof2(map->limit, MEGABYTE));
       goto retry;
